          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Years and Education</strong><br>\nHector Berlioz was a French composer born in 1803 who initially studied medicine before turning to music. He attended the Paris Conservatoire and was influenced by the works of Beethoven and Shakespeare.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Symphonie Fantastique</strong><br>\nBerlioz's breakthrough came with \"Symphonie Fantastique\" in 1830, which introduced a new concert experience with its vivid storytelling and use of an idée fixe, a recurring musical theme that represents the protagonist's obsessive love.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Contributions to Program Music</strong><br>\nBerlioz is considered a pioneer of program music, which evokes a narrative or non-musical idea. His compositions often tell a story or paint a scene, extending the range of what instrumental music could express.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Literary Inspirations</strong><br>\nMany of Berlioz's works were inspired by literary sources, with compositions based on the works of Virgil, Goethe, and Lord Byron. This intersection of music and literature was a hallmark of the Romantic era.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Opera and Choral Works</strong><br>\nBeyond symphonies, Berlioz also composed operas, choral works, and a vast array of other pieces. His opera \"Les Troyens\" is one of his most ambitious works, based on the Aeneid by Virgil.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Innovations in Orchestration</strong><br>\nBerlioz was an innovative orchestrator who expanded the orchestra's capabilities. He wrote a treatise on instrumentation, which became a cornerstone for composers in understanding and utilizing the orchestra.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
